{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>For lying down.</b> It gives a heh (the definite article), and in the passage of Kiddushin, לרבעה with a weak (raphe) heh." "<b>A tevel (perversion) it is.</b> By the word שורק it indicates about it its companion [i.e., the preceding clause], both in masculine language."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The comment refers to the heh of לרבעה being read as the definite article in the talmudic passage in tractate Kiddushin; 'ודפרשת קדושים' literally means 'and that which was expounded in Kiddushin.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:13:16.600944468Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}